  "selectors": [
    {
      "root_table": "teams",
      "scope": [],
      "focal": {
        "path": [
          "teams",
          "user_teams",
          "users",
          "channel_members",
          "channels"
        ],
        "joins": [
          "user_teams.team_id",
          "user_teams.user_id",
          "channel_members.user_id",
          "channel_members.channel_id"
        ],
        "filters": [
          {
            "node": 1,
            "field": "role",
            "op": "eq",
            "value": "admin"
          },
          {
            "node": 4,
            "field": "channel_name",
            "op": "eq",
            "value": "on-call"
          }
        ]
      },
      "auxiliary": []
    }
  ],
  "negative_referents": [
    "T03SUMMIT",
    "T04VERTEX",
    "T01WORKSPACE"
  ],
  "notes": "Selector anchors user_teams to the root team via the FK team_id (node0->node1), which forces the admin-role check to be evaluated within that same workspace's membership record before following that specific admin user to their channel memberships and checking for an exact 'on-call' channel name. This correctly matches Northstar (Priyanka Rao) and Lumen (Marcus Webb), and correctly excludes Summit (its on-call member Priyanka's admin role is tied to Northstar's user_teams row, not Summit's), Vertex (no admin row exists there), and the base Test Workspace (its admins Robert Walsh/Morgan Freeman are not members of C_ONCALL_T01). Actor U01AGENBOT9 was given workspace membership in all four new teams and channel membership in every on-call channel (plus the incident-response distractor) so that conversations.list (per team_id), conversations.members, and users.info are all reachable through documented APIs without relying on hidden seed knowledge. No messages were needed for this obligation."
}
